# Page Template Location

Store custom WordPress page templates in `page-templates/` instead of the theme root.

## Required conventions

- Create new custom page templates in `page-templates/`.
- Do not add new `page-*.php` template files at the theme root.
- When editing existing root-level custom templates, prefer moving them into `page-templates/` in the same change when safe.
- Preserve the `Template Name:` header and behavior when moving templates.

## Notes

- This rule applies to custom page templates, not core hierarchy files like `page.php`, `single.php`, `single-coach.php`, `404.php`, or `index.php`.
- This theme has no custom page templates yet: every page is `page.php` plus its Hero Content and Page sections fields.
